cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, or GeoJSON it produced, in research or in a publication,
  please cite it as below. The code is MIT-licensed; the citation is how attribution is asked for.
title: "fire-insurance-maps: georeferencing historical fire insurance plans from the text printed on them"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Farr
    given-names: Chloe
    affiliation: University of Victoria, Leibniz TIB
  - family-names: Hurd
    given-names: Emilia
    affiliation: University of Victoria
date-released: "2026-09-20"
version: "2026.09.20"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/chloe-farr/fire-insurance-maps-geotagger"
keywords:
  - fire insurance plans
  - Goad
  - Sanborn
  - georeferencing
  - OCR
  - historical GIS
abstract: >-
  Reads every word on a scanned fire insurance plan with an open-weight OCR model, traces the
  city blocks and building outlines from the linework, matches the street names to present-day
  street centrelines and fits the sheet to the Earth from those matches alone, writing blocks,
  buildings, words and the sheet outline as GeoJSON with a world file.
